# Local-only: HTTPS in front of MinIO, so the local production stack can be driven from a real
# browser rather than only from curl.
#
# Why it has to exist. The app is served from https://localhost:8443, and the phone (or the
# browser) uploads media *directly* to object storage with a presigned PUT. A fetch from an https
# page to an http endpoint is blocked as mixed content, so http://localhost:9100 is unusable from
# the app even though it is a perfectly good MinIO. Terminating TLS in front of MinIO at
# https://localhost:9443 removes that, and it rehearses the exact production shape: storage on
# its own hostname, reached over https, with Storage__PublicEndpoint pointing at it.
#
# The Host header is passed through unchanged — Caddy's default — and that is load-bearing.
# SigV4 signs the host, so if this proxy rewrote it, every presigned URL the API hands out would
# fail authentication for a reason nothing in the error message would mention.
#
# Production equivalent: the commented `media.{$TEREN_DOMAIN}` block at the bottom of
# deploy/Caddyfile, and only if you self-host storage instead of using Hetzner Object Storage.

{
	local_certs
}

https://localhost:9443 {
	tls internal
	reverse_proxy minio:9000
}
